{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/510314-the-horror-of-powers-do-you-use-it","id":510314,"title":"The horror of powers; do you use it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-10T19:35:26-07:00","id":510314,"title":"The horror of powers; do you use it?","content":"I'm kind of new to Hunter storytelling (or, really, storytelling as a whole), but I was wondering something. Monsters have a lot of strange and unnatural powers inherent to them, especially if you go for the complexities of the crossover route. I was just wondering; do you ever use those powers to try and get the &quot;feel&quot; of hunting - the horror of facing something so clearly wrong and out of this world?<br /> <br /> I mean, I may be barking up the wrong tree here, but when I read the 2e description of Mistform for VtR, I immediately thought of a scene like this:<br /> <br /> <i>The faintest whisper is the only hint that something is wrong, that your prey has snuck up behind you. Thick white vapor, a writhing cloud of mist, seeps quietly from the vents, wafting almost lazily through the air. It moves across the floor, tangling around your buddy's legs, and then, unnaturally, it rises up, intangible tendrils enveloping your friend. He shouts in alarm and lashes out with his stake, thrusting and swinging the carved bit of 2X4, but it does nothing; his blows merely pass through the smokey substance. Greedily, it draws itself around him, enveloping him like a shroud, and pours down his open mouth and his nose.<br /> <br /> He claws at his face, muffled screams bubbling out, but the mist can't be moved. You try to help, to drag him out of its cold, clammy embrace, but in vein; it clings to him like jelly, even as it defies your own efforts to remove it.<br /> <br /> All you can do is watch, helpless, as he sinks to his knees, struggles growing weaker as the once-white mist begins to turn a thick, bloody red.<br /> <br /> Moments later, he is still. The gory cloud hovering above his corpse - grotesquely shriveled, as if he had somehow been sucked dry - and then, it starts to drift purposely towards you, long tendrils reaching out for you in turn...</i><br /> <br /> And then there was this scene that came to mind after reading in 2e WtF that werewolves <b>only</b> take Agg damage from silver and magic, and even &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot; only inflicts Lethal damage... to say nothing of the fact that Garou form regenerates <b>all</b> Lethal + all Bashing damage at the start of each turn...<br /> <br /> <i><br /> You duck and cover as the shockwave rolls over you, the thunder of the homemade explosion mingling with the crashing of stone as the hut comes crashing down on the man-beast inside of it. As you pick yourselves up and start to congratulate yourselves on ending it, an inhuman howl of pain and fury echoes from beneath the timber. Boards shatter and heave as a lumbering shape forces its way up from beneath. In the flickering light of burning wood, you can seek the twisted, mangled figure of your foe. Its limbs are shattered and bent, its flesh torn and burnt. Organs spill from its rent belly, half of its head is deflated, and yet, grotesquely, it's still alive.<br /> <br /> It hurls lumber aside and strides towards you, ungainly on twisted legs. Before your eyes, its body begins to heal; entrails curling back into its midriff, bones audibly crunching as they twist back into alignment, flesh reknitting. Within seconds, it is as if you had never even touched it. It throws back its bestial head and bays at the full moon above, then drops to all fours and charges at you.<br /> </i><br /> <br /> So, I may be wrong, but to me, this seem like horrifying scenes. Reminders of just what sorts of unearthly, unnatural creatures that a hunter is going up against, and their nature as a small and frail speck by comparison.<br /> <br /> Is this a &quot;proper&quot; approach to horror? If it is, have you ever used it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T22:19:59-07:00","id":510455,"title":"","content":"there is indeed a proper approach, and dont you DARE do it wrong, every knows that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Joking aside, i dont think there is a proper approach, but your writing certainly sets a much more horror feel than something in one of my games &quot;The werewolf takes 8 lethal as you blow the house up, he spends essence to heal as he comes out from under the rubble and in death rage charges at you.&quot; &quot;Who has the silver loaded shotgun? Brian?&quot; &quot;Yea, lure him into the pit so i can get a clean head shot from up above. Do we need to roll for lunacy or anything?&quot; ...etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2741-hemophage","name":"Hemophage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:08:26-07:00","id":510527,"title":"","content":"I am of a different stroke. I entirely think that Voiddrifters approach is correct and pretty cool - even though I hate the Werewolf healing rules, as they stand - and I actually think, sorry in advance, think that Hemophages approach is incorrect. It isn't very moody and feels much too mechanic and &quot;gamey&quot;. If you and your friends are having fun with it, I wont try to tell you to do otherwise, but I dont anyone I've ever played WoD would consider that approach anything but stale and boring.<br /> <br /> I try to incorporate the horror of the supernatural, even in games where the players themselves are playing the supernatural creatures. I often play very loose with mechanics in order to facillitate this. Like one of my players in a Sin-Eater game, who activated the Phantasmal Cual turning into an avalance of wet flesh and gnashing teeth to punish a child rapist.<br /> Its important to remember that the supernatural creatures in the WoD are still monsters in some respect, and their powers should portray this. This is dobly important in Hunter, where you dont really have anything other than your own gumption, gusto and bravado to see you through. Atleast for the most part.<br /> If I ever ran a Hunter game, I think I would take alot of inspiration from the Lovecraft portrays monster hunting. Its possible and doable, but its bloody dangerous and one wrong move at the wrong time, will get you murdered, driven insane or worse. These are monsters, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:14:51-07:00","id":510555,"title":"","content":"The second dot of protean lets you wall crawl now. Nice horror movie stuff right there if you can pull of a spider-vamp ceiling stalker routine. And maybe just wait til the hunters are off-guard and just kinda drop on one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:00:57-07:00","id":513186,"title":"","content":"Domination, the Mind arcanum... Any obvious use of mental powers over a helpess, conditioned v\u00edctim is a sure way to make your characters feel disturbed without cheap gore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:31:53-07:00","id":514209,"title":"","content":"I rob my players of their sense of reality; I play an unreliable narrator. They get admitted to a hospital that won't be opened for another week; the man whose car they stop has a corpse sitting in the passenger seat.<br /> <br /> They all dream of the ocean. When they wake up, the hospital is entirely empty except for them. The unicorns on the wallpaper of the children's ward are just horses with spikes stabbed into their heads (or maybe the horses were just unicorns who had their horns removed; I honestly can't recall).<br /> <br /> You can still see the blood. And when the tick-tock man comes for you, and your first response is to dive into the sewers to get away from how he shoves you out of time...<br /> <br /> I dunno, I don't think I've used the horror of powers; I've always just stuck with Dada and giving my players enough rope to hang themselves with.<br /> <br /> After all, I'm a lot more concerned about <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JaLjwSpZ6Cs\" target=\"_blank\">what he's building in there</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:55:14-07:00","id":514444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/510314-the-horror-of-powers-do-you-use-it?p=510555#post510555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second dot of protean lets you wall crawl now. Nice horror movie stuff right there if you can pull of a spider-vamp ceiling stalker routine. And maybe just wait til the hunters are off-guard and just kinda drop on one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my new players is NEW TO WORLD OF DARKNESS (WOOOT) when asked his five questions it turns out that he was once a cop who lost his job after he shot a serial killer in the middle of mutilating a victim... only for it to turn out to be the guy's kid.<br /> <br /> that was the worst thing he's ever done. its actually worse than the thing he could imagine himself doing.<br /> <br /> it is not worse than what he forgot, though. what he forgot is that that boy he shot in the head wasn't a boy, it was a thing that looked like a boy but it had black eyes and teeth like a shark and it was gnawing on the man's throat.<br /> <br /> What he doesn't know is that that thing that looked like a boy followed him to Louisiana and is looking for him. <br /> <br /> Vic's built for grapple attacks and when the boy (a Gangrel... shhh) attacks, I expect him to get thrown against the wall only to scramble up it like a spider, in fact all of the boy's movements will be spider/marionette like... its got humanity 1 after all.<br /> <br /> the thing isn't strong, it isn't fast, not really, but it will not stop coming for him. Ever. Not until he figures out its a vampire (which will not be easy... the thing takes huge bites out of its victims and leaves lots of blood behind) and stakes it OR becomes our chronicle's token evil teammate (mwahahaha).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:59:22-07:00","id":514446,"title":"","content":"As for the actual topic in general: I tend to do a mix of the OP and the second post, new stuff is intense afterwards I like to let the players get a little jaded, then I start doing what Amechra does, nonchalantely mention them walking by a guy they know's dead, or make them make odd empathy/streetwise checks when interacting with allies, make them have strangely out of character mishaps... leave's the players convince maybe something/nothing's about to go wrong when in fact EVERYTHING HAS ALREADY GONE TITS UP. I'm not allowed to do scary things after 10pm anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:46:18-07:00","id":514522,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which: Anyone successfully give their players the heebee jeebees? <br /> <br /> I'm not allowed to talked about winged eyes anymore, and the current haunted University story actually unnerved my super-jaded laughs at the Chainsaw Massacre Remake player (Internet High Five), another less jaded player kept my wife on the phone on the way home &quot;just in case&quot; mwahahaha. <br /> <br /> I wanna do it again: How have you done it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:59:31-07:00","id":514533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/510314-the-horror-of-powers-do-you-use-it?p=514522#post514522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which: Anyone successfully give their players the heebee jeebees?<br /> <br /> I'm not allowed to talked about winged eyes anymore, and the current haunted University story actually unnerved my super-jaded laughs at the Chainsaw Massacre Remake player (Internet High Five), another less jaded player kept my wife on the phone on the way home &quot;just in case&quot; mwahahaha.<br /> <br /> I wanna do it again: How have you done it?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my players still shudders about something I &quot;made&quot; her do. Basically, she loves rats IRL, and so did her character.<br /> <br /> So they were down in the sewers, and there were these massive flowers that smelled like rotting meat; you could hear the sounds of rats swarming and squeaking inside.<br /> <br /> So she decided that she wanted to get them out (she got the impression that the flower was eating the rats, instead of the other way around); so she pulled out her lighter (IC) and said she wanted to light the flower on fire.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you <i>sure</i> you want to do that?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> &quot;You just set the flower full of rats on fire. They're all dying in front of you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;worst thing she could imagine doing&quot; was killing a rat. She killed <i>hundreds</i>. She still feels bad about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}